-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III (Terrorist Property) -- NOUNS, layer 1.
--
-- Types only: DECLARE and nothing else.  No rule, no #EVAL.  Every other ta-*.l4 module imports this one.
-- The membership test (encoding-a-subject, step 4): could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this
-- fact, or does answering it require reading the Act?  Only the first kind is here.  Whether those facts make
-- a person guilty, protected, obliged or entitled is a rule, and lives in the module of the section that says so.
--
-- Terms the Act borrows from outside Part III are facts here, never worked out: "for the purposes of
-- terrorism" (section 1 of the Act, not among the sources), "proscribed organisation", "a business in the
-- regulated sector" (Schedule 3A), "statutory maximum", "level 5 on the standard scale", bank holidays (the
-- Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971), "equivalent money laundering requirements", "group" (a Directive),
-- "ancillary offence" and "terrorist connection" (the Counter-Terrorism Act 2008), "privileged information".
--
-- Field names start at the complement (the genitive 's supplies the verb), so a record field is read as
-- `the act's invites another to provide it`.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Which of the offences created by sections 15 to 18 (and 17A, for section 23 only) is meant.
DECLARE `Offence of Part III` IS ONE OF
    `an offence under s 15(1)`
    `an offence under s 15(2)`
    `an offence under s 15(3)`
    `an offence under s 16(1)`
    `an offence under s 16(2)`
    `an offence under s 17`
    `an offence under s 17A`
    `an offence under s 18`

-- How a person is convicted; the penalties of sections 19(8), 21A(12), 21D(4) and 22 differ by route.
DECLARE `Conviction route` IS ONE OF
    `on conviction on indictment`
    `on summary conviction`

-- Section 22B(1) and (1A): the court that is asked for an information order, and (s 22D(3)) the court that hears an appeal.
DECLARE `Court that decided` IS ONE OF
    `a magistrates court in England and Wales`
    `a magistrates court in Northern Ireland`
    `the sheriff`

DECLARE `Appeal court` IS ONE OF
    `the Crown Court`
    `a county court`
    `the Sheriff Appeal Court`

-- Section 21(5): the offences under which the defence is limited to a list.
-- Section 22B(14): "terrorist financing" differs by subsection.
DECLARE `Conditions of s 22B` IS ONE OF
    `Condition 1`
    `Condition 2`
    `Condition 3`
    `Condition 4`

-- Section 21CA(2)(c), 21CF(6): the kinds of relevant undertaking.
DECLARE `Kind of relevant undertaking` IS ONE OF
    `a credit institution`
    `a financial institution`
    `a professional legal adviser`
    `a relevant professional adviser`
    `another person whose business consists of activities listed in paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 3A`
    `none of these`

-- Section 21CC(7), 21CD: who made the required notification.
DECLARE `Who made the notification` IS ONE OF
    `Person A`
    `Person B`

-- Section 21CC(7): who asked for the disclosure.
DECLARE `Who asked for the disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `a constable`
    `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Penalties: a ceiling is a ceiling, never an amount to be paid
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A fine ceiling is either a stated amount (the amount itself comes from outside the Act: the statutory
-- maximum, level 5 on the standard scale) or no ceiling is stated in the text.
DECLARE `Fine ceiling` IS ONE OF
    `No ceiling is stated`
    `A fine not exceeding` HAS amount IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Penalty ceiling` HAS
    `longest term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `fine` IS A `Fine ceiling`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Section 14: terrorist property
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Proceeds facts` HAS
    `it is the proceeds of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it represents the proceeds of the act, wholly or partly, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a payment or other reward in connection with the act's commission` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Property facts` HAS
    `likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied or made available, or to be applied or made available, for use by a proscribed organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism` IS A `Proceeds facts`
    `proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism` IS A `Proceeds facts`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 15 to 18: what a person did, and what was in their mind
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Mind about use for terrorism` HAS
    `intends that it should be used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows that it will be used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Fund-raising act` HAS
    `invites another to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lends it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `otherwise makes it available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Use and possession act` HAS
    `uses it for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Arrangement act` HAS
    `enters into an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `becomes concerned in an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result money or other property is or is to be made available to another` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Laundering act` HAS
    `enters into an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `becomes concerned in an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person by concealment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person by removal from the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person by transfer to nominees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person in any other way` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 17A(1): the insurer's payment.
DECLARE `Insurance payment facts` HAS
    `the person is the insurer under an insurance contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment made under the contract or purportedly under it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment in respect of money or other property handed over or to be handed over in response to a demand made wholly or partly for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that it was or is to be handed over in response to such a demand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person authorising the payment on the insurer's behalf knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that it was or is to be handed over in response to such a demand` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 17A(2) to (4): the officer or partner of a body that committed the offence.
DECLARE `Officer liability facts` HAS
    `offence under s 17A committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `offence under s 17A committed by a Scottish partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved to have been committed with the person's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved to be attributable to neglect on the person's part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was purporting to act in such a capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 17A(5): the insurance contract.
DECLARE `Contract facts` HAS
    `one party accepts significant insurance risk from another party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by agreeing to compensate the other party if a specified uncertain future event adversely affects that party` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 18(2): what the accused proves.
DECLARE `Proof about terrorist property` HAS
    `proves that he did not know that the arrangement related to terrorist property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proves that he had no reasonable cause to suspect that the arrangement related to terrorist property` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 19 to 21ZC: telling the police
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Section 19(1): a person who believes or suspects, from information that came to them at work.
DECLARE `Information facts` HAS
    `believes or suspects that another person has committed an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bases the belief or suspicion on information that came in the course of a trade, profession or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bases the belief or suspicion on information that came in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information came in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What the person has disclosed to a constable.
DECLARE `Disclosure facts` HAS
    `discloses to a constable the belief or suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discloses to a constable the information on which it is based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as soon as is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 19(4): the employer's procedure.
DECLARE `Procedure facts` HAS
    `the person is in employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is charged with the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person disclosed in accordance with the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 19(6), 21A(8): how information reaches a legal adviser.
DECLARE `Privilege facts` HAS
    `it came otherwise than with a view to furthering a criminal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it came from a client or a client's representative in connection with the provision of legal advice by the adviser to the client` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it came from a person seeking legal advice from the adviser, or from the person's representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it came from any person for the purpose of actual or contemplated legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 19(7), 21A(11): an act abroad that would have been an offence in the United Kingdom.
DECLARE `Act abroad facts` HAS
    `the person has taken an action or been in possession of a thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person would have committed an offence under one of sections 15 to 18 if in the United Kingdom at the time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 19(7B), 20(5), 21A(14), 21B(7), 21CF(2): who counts as "a constable".
DECLARE `Officer facts` HAS
    `a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of the section by the Director General of that Agency` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 22A: employment.
DECLARE `Employment facts` HAS
    `any employment, whether paid or unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `work under a contract for services or as an office-holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `work experience provided pursuant to a training course or programme or in the course of training for employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntary work` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21(2) to (4): the person's involvement and what they disclosed.
DECLARE `Cooperation facts` HAS
    `involved in a transaction or arrangement relating to money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discloses to a constable the suspicion or belief that the money or other property is terrorist property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discloses to a constable the information on which the suspicion or belief is based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `makes the disclosure after he becomes concerned in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `makes the disclosure on his own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `makes the disclosure as soon as is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a constable forbids him to continue his involvement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he continues his involvement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21ZA(1): prior consent.
DECLARE `Prior consent facts` HAS
    `involved in a transaction or an arrangement relating to money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before becoming involved, discloses to an authorised officer the suspicion or belief that the money or other property is terrorist property and the information on which it is based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the authorised officer's consent to becoming involved` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21ZB(1) to (3): disclosure after becoming involved.
DECLARE `Later disclosure facts` HAS
    `involved in a transaction or an arrangement relating to money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `after becoming involved, discloses to an authorised officer the suspicion or belief and the information on which it is based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable excuse for the failure to make the disclosure before becoming involved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is made on the person's own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is made as soon as it is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised officer forbids the person to continue involvement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person continues that involvement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 21A to 21C and 21H: the regulated sector
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Section 21A(2) to (4): the three conditions.
DECLARE `Regulated sector facts` HAS
    `knows or suspects that another person has committed or attempted to commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person has committed or attempted to commit such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information or other matter came to him in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discloses the information or other matter to a constable or a nominated officer as soon as is practicable after it comes to him` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21A(5): the exceptions.
DECLARE `Exception facts` HAS
    `a reasonable excuse for not disclosing the information or other matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a professional legal adviser or relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information or other matter came to him in privileged circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21A(5A): a person who assists an adviser.
DECLARE `Assistance facts` HAS
    `employed by, or in partnership with, a professional legal adviser or relevant professional adviser to provide the adviser with assistance or support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information or other matter comes to the person in connection with the provision of such assistance or support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information or other matter came to the adviser in privileged circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21A(6): guidance the court must consider.
DECLARE `Guidance facts` HAS
    `issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published in a manner the Treasury approved as appropriate to bring it to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relevant guidance which was at the time concerned` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21A(7), 21B(5): a disclosure to a nominated officer.
DECLARE `Nominated officer facts` HAS
    `made to a person nominated by the employer to receive disclosures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the course of the discloser's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in accordance with the procedure the employer established for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21A(8) and (9): privileged circumstances.
DECLARE `Adviser communication facts` HAS
    `communicated or given by a client of the adviser, or a representative, in connection with the giving of legal advice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `communicated or given by a person seeking legal advice from the adviser, or a representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `communicated or given by a person in connection with legal proceedings or contemplated legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `communicated or given with a view to furthering a criminal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21A(15), 21H(5): a relevant professional adviser.
DECLARE `Professional adviser facts` HAS
    `an accountant, auditor or tax adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of a professional body established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers (as the case may be)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership as a condition for admission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, and sanctions for non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21B(1) to (4): a protected disclosure.
DECLARE `Protected disclosure facts` HAS
    `the information or other matter came to the discloser in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information causes the discloser to know or suspect that another person has committed or attempted to commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information gives the discloser reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person has committed or attempted to commit such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is made to a constable or a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is made as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter comes to the discloser` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 21CA to 21CF: voluntary disclosures within the regulated sector
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Section 21CA(2): condition 1.
DECLARE `Condition 1 facts` HAS
    `A is carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information on which the disclosure is based came to A in the course of carrying on that business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each person to whom the information is to be disclosed is also carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CA(3): condition 2.
DECLARE `Request facts` HAS
    `a constable has requested A to make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person to whom the information is to be disclosed (or at least one of them) has requested A to do so` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CA(5): condition 4.
DECLARE `Assist facts` HAS
    `A is satisfied that the disclosure will or may assist in determining a matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is involved in the commission of a terrorist financing offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `A is satisfied that the disclosure will or may assist in determining a matter in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CB(1): what every disclosure request must contain.
DECLARE `Request content facts` HAS
    `states that it is made in connection with a suspicion of involvement in a terrorist financing offence or the identification of terrorist property or its movement or use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the person or property so far as known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the information that is sought from A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the person or persons to whom it is requested that the information is disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CB(2) to (4): the extra content of a request made by a person mentioned in section 21CA(3)(b).
DECLARE `Recipient request facts` HAS
    `the request is made by a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request states that it is made in connection with a suspicion of involvement in a terrorist financing offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request states that it is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request sets out the grounds for the suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request provides such other information as the person making it thinks appropriate for enabling A to determine whether the information ought to be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CB(7): the required notification where the request came from another undertaking.
DECLARE `Requester notification facts` HAS
    `states that a disclosure request has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the person to whom the request was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request is made in connection with a suspicion of involvement in a terrorist financing offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person suspected is known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the person suspected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder of the property is known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the property and the person who holds it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CB(8): the notification a requester gives before making the request (condition 5).
DECLARE `Advance notification facts` HAS
    `states that a disclosure request is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the person to whom it is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the information to be sought in the request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `explains why the request is being made` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CC(1): when the section applies.
DECLARE `Section 21CC applies facts` HAS
    `a question arises in proceedings as to whether the required disclosure has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a person who discloses information under s 21CA(1) as a result of a disclosure request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a person who makes a required notification in accordance with s 21CB(5)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by any other person to whom A discloses information under s 21CA(1) as a result of that request` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CC(5): the content of a joint disclosure report about a suspicion.
DECLARE `Suspicion report content facts` HAS
    `explains the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the person is involved in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out the grounds for the suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides any other information relevant to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CC(6): the content of a joint disclosure report about terrorist property.
DECLARE `Property report content facts` HAS
    `explains the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the property is terrorist property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property and the person who holds it are known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the property and the person who holds it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `details of its movement or use are known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides details of its movement or use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides any other information relevant to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21CC(9): approval and signature of a joint disclosure report.
DECLARE `Report approval facts` HAS
    `there is a nominated officer of each person that jointly makes the report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the nominated officer of each such person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the nominated officer on behalf of each such person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved and signed by another senior officer` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 21D to 21H: tipping off in the regulated sector
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Section 21D(2): the matters a person must not disclose.
DECLARE `Protected matter facts` HAS
    `the person or another person has made a disclosure under a provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure was made to a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure was made in accordance with a procedure established by that person's employer for the making of disclosures under that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure was made to a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure was made to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of that provision by the Director General of that Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure was of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21D(1) (b) and (c).
DECLARE `Tipping off facts` HAS
    `the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted following the disclosure referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21D(3).
DECLARE `Investigation disclosure facts` HAS
    `the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21E(2): a disclosure within a group of institutions.
DECLARE `Group disclosure facts` HAS
    `the disclosure is by a credit institution or a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is to a credit institution or a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both the institution making the disclosure and the institution to whom it is made belong to the same group` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21E(4): a disclosure between advisers in undertakings under common ownership, management or control.
DECLARE `Adviser group facts` HAS
    `the person making the disclosure is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is to a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both the person making the disclosure and the person to whom it is made carry on business in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those persons perform their professional activities within different undertakings that share common ownership, management or control` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21F(1): the disclosures to which section 21F applies.
DECLARE `Between institutions facts` HAS
    `by a credit institution to another credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a financial institution to another financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a professional legal adviser to another professional legal adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a relevant professional adviser of a particular kind to another relevant professional adviser of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21F(2).
DECLARE `Institution disclosure facts` HAS
    `the disclosure relates to a client or former client of the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure relates to a transaction involving them both` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure relates to the provision of a service involving them both` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is for the purpose only of preventing an offence under this Part of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution or adviser to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made are subject to equivalent duties of professional confidentiality and the protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 21G(1).
DECLARE `Permitted disclosure facts` HAS
    `the disclosure is to the authority that is the supervisory authority for that person by virtue of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is made in good faith by virtue of s 21CA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is for the purpose of the detection, investigation or prosecution of a criminal offence (whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is for the purpose of an investigation under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is for the purpose of the enforcement of any order of a court under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 22B to 22F: information orders
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Section 22B(4): condition 1.
DECLARE `Info order condition 1 facts` HAS
    `the information required would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under s 21A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respondent is the person who made the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respondent is otherwise carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information would assist in investigating whether a person is involved in the commission of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 or in determining whether an investigation of that kind should be started` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information would assist in identifying terrorist property or its movement or use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 22B(5): condition 2.
DECLARE `Info order condition 2 facts` HAS
    `the information required would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under a corresponding disclosure requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an external request has been made to the National Crime Agency for the provision of information in connection with that disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respondent is carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is likely to be of substantial value to the authority that made the external request in determining any matter in connection with the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 22B(6A): condition 3.
DECLARE `Info order condition 3 facts` HAS
    `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct operational analysis of information that is relevant to terrorist financing or suspected terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of terrorist financing, or systemic deficiencies or vulnerabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that analysis is for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency so far as it relates to terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made to a magistrates court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made to the sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 22B(6B): condition 4.
DECLARE `Info order condition 4 facts` HAS
    `a request has been made by a foreign FIU to the National Crime Agency for the provision of the information required to be given under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the request was made only for the purpose of assisting the foreign FIU to conduct operational or strategic analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the information is likely to be of substantial value to the foreign FIU in carrying out such analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provision of the information by the National Crime Agency to the foreign FIU would be for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function so far as it relates to terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made to a magistrates court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made to the sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sections 23 to 23B: forfeiture
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Section 23(2) to (7): the facts about one item of money or other property.
DECLARE `Forfeitable property facts` HAS
    `at the time of the offence the person had it in their possession or under their control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person intended that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person had reasonable cause to suspect that it might be used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew or had reasonable cause to suspect that it would or might be used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement in question related to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was received by any person as a payment or other reward in connection with the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the amount paid under, or purportedly under, the insurance contract` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 23A(1): the conditions for property after a terrorism-related conviction.
DECLARE `Terrorism forfeiture facts` HAS
    `it was, at the time of the offence, in the possession or control of the person convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was intended by that person that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court believes that it will be used for the purposes of terrorism unless forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 23A(2): the offences to which section 23A applies.
DECLARE `Offence listed in s 23A(2)` IS ONE OF
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 54 (weapons training)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 57 (possessing things for the purposes of terrorism)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 58 (collecting information for the purposes of terrorism)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 58A (collecting information for the purposes of terrorism)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 58B (entering or remaining in a designated area)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 59 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 60 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom)`
    `Terrorism Act 2000 section 61 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom)`
    `Terrorism Act 2006 section 2 (dissemination of terrorist publications)`
    `Terrorism Act 2006 section 5 (preparation of terrorist acts)`
    `Terrorism Act 2006 section 6 (training for terrorism)`
    `Terrorism Act 2006 section 9 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials)`
    `Terrorism Act 2006 section 10 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials)`
    `Terrorism Act 2006 section 11 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials)`
    `none of these`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulative rules: who must, may or shall not do what
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Party under Part III` IS ONE OF
    `the person`
    `a constable`
    `the respondent`
    `the Secretary of State`
    `the court`
    `a law enforcement officer`
    `the person who made the required notification`
    `the person in the regulated sector`

DECLARE `Act under Part III` IS ONE OF
    `disclose the belief or suspicion and the information to a constable`
    `disclose the matter to a constable`
    `disclose the disclosure in full to an authorised National Crime Agency officer`
    `notify a constable that a joint disclosure report is not being made`
    `provide the information the order requires`
    `give an opportunity to be heard`
    `make an application for an information order`
    `include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency`
    `disclose a matter that is likely to prejudice an investigation`
    `consider whether the person followed the relevant guidance`
    `have regard to the value of the property and the likely effects of the order on the convicted person`
    `make a forfeiture order in Scotland other than on the application of the prosecutor`
